(5933593, 864910, 97166, '<td valign="top">Bold move to keep the shirt saturated, as it''ll probably get hit hard by the anti-desat movement that''s about these days.<br/> <br/>Personally, I would have kept the eyes saturated as well to help balance the photo out, although if they''re hazel/brown/etc. it wouldn''t have mattered much. In which case I would have kept the shirt B&amp;W.  There''s a bit of an issue with composition balance as well, as the upper part of the photo doesn''t really add much, and takes away from the feel.<br/> <br/>Not saying, of course, that you should do these things, but that''s how I feel when I look at it.</td>', 'Bold move to keep the shirt saturated, as it''ll probably get hit hard by the anti-desat movement that''s about these days. Personally, I would have kept the eyes saturated as well to help balance the photo out, although if they''re hazel/brown/etc. it wouldn''t have mattered much. In which case I would have kept the shirt B&W.  There''s a bit of an issue with composition balance as well, as the upper part of the photo doesn''t really add much, and takes away from the feel. Not saying, of course, that you should do these things, but that''s how I feel when I look at it.', '2010-04-06 15:17:31.000000', NULL, 1),
(5933595, 865051, 97166, '<td valign="top">Sepia tone here, IMO, is a little too strong for the wistful nature of the photo. The warmth is good, but it''s fighting too much with the playful nature of the photo, wanting to give it a darker, more antiquish feel which I don''t much care for.</td>', 'Sepia tone here, IMO, is a little too strong for the wistful nature of the photo. The warmth is good, but it''s fighting too much with the playful nature of the photo, wanting to give it a darker, more antiquish feel which I don''t much care for.', '2010-04-06 15:19:13.000000', NULL, 1),
(5933597, 865153, 97166, '<td valign="top">I like the various stages of focus here, nicely done.  I can''t help but wonder what this would look like with a nice B&amp;W conversion.</td>', 'I like the various stages of focus here, nicely done.  I can''t help but wonder what this would look like with a nice B&W conversion.', '2010-04-06 15:21:26.000000', NULL, 1),
(5933601, 864991, 97166, '<td valign="top">A nice studio study.  I tend to like these more when the child is focused on interacting with the environment, however, than directly with the photographer, unless cropped/framed closer in.  Personal preference, of course, just a note.</td>', 'A nice studio study.  I tend to like these more when the child is focused on interacting with the environment, however, than directly with the photographer, unless cropped/framed closer in.  Personal preference, of course, just a note.', '2010-04-06 15:22:55.000000', NULL, 1),
(5933604, 864972, 97166, '<td valign="top">Certainly different, focusing on something other than the child''s face/expression/etc, but not so sure if it works for me.</td>', 'Certainly different, focusing on something other than the child''s face/expression/etc, but not so sure if it works for me.', '2010-04-06 15:24:11.000000', NULL, 1),
(5933606, 864926, 97166, '<td valign="top">Hah. 7 for the humor alone. An extra point for being shot rather well.</td>', 'Hah. 7 for the humor alone. An extra point for being shot rather well.', '2010-04-06 15:24:40.000000', NULL, 1),
(5933609, 865092, 97166, '<td valign="top">I like this. It''s an imaginative take, and a risk worth entering.</td>', 'I like this. It''s an imaginative take, and a risk worth entering.', '2010-04-06 15:25:13.000000', NULL, 1),
(5933614, 865177, 97166, '<td valign="top">I need to start photographing more like this. It''s a style that really speaks to me. If this isn''t Rinac''s, then whoever it is is channeling her nicely.</td>', 'I need to start photographing more like this. It''s a style that really speaks to me. If this isn''t Rinac''s, then whoever it is is channeling her nicely.', '2010-04-06 15:27:24.000000', NULL, 1),
